- op: discuss  # 40ff
  at: '2026-03-19T00:49:45Z'  # 40ff
  by: agent  # 40ff
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 40ff
  clock: 10  # 40ff
  nonce: 40ff  # 40ff
  message: "Correction: the suffix index is already hash-based (built lazily on first use). _lookup_suffix is O(1) per call, not O(n). Re-profiling killbill post-optimization:\n\nTop bottleneck: iter_tree at 9.9s (11M function calls) — this is the generic tree-sitter node iterator. For Flink's ~88M calls, this would be ~80s alone. The overhead is Python function call overhead for each node visit.\n\nOptions for Flink improvement:\n1. Cython/C extension for iter_tree (~10x faster, but adds build complexity)\n2. Avoid full tree iteration in extract_edges — only visit nodes of specific types\n3. Use tree-sitter cursor API instead of recursive children walk\n4. Accept 25-30 min for repos with 14K+ files as a known limitation\n\nThe hash-based resolver hypothesis was wrong. The actual bottleneck is tree traversal overhead."  # 40ff
